R50 a month. We pull ten thousand rand into the house between my gogo’s pension and the child support grant. School fees already take between R4 001 and R8 000 of that every year. The rest covers the forty-five minute taxi I catch each way, food, and whatever’s left when the taps run dry or the power cuts stretch past the schedule. You’re asking me to hand over another monthly charge for an app that promises to turn study hours into cash. I’ve heard that exact pitch before. It never lands. I might want a platform that actually pays out, but wanting it doesn’t stretch a rand. Fifty rand a month is a recurring hit I can’t absorb. Show me it works without charging upfront, or don’t touch the budget at all.

