I really like the idea of getting rewarded for studying, especially when walking past those same crime-heavy streets in Mthatha makes me wish I had a safer, more focused reason to stay indoors, but R50 a month is R600 a year that my ma and I need for groceries and transport. I can’t justify pulling that from our household budget, even though I want the extra motivation, because that recurring cost directly competes with our real essentials. I would only reconsider if you let me earn the subscription fee through a free trial first, so I’m not risking my family’s money on an app I haven’t seen work.
